  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assistance and Protection to Vulnerable Migrants in Bosnia and Herzegovina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2017, mixed migration flows have increased significantly in the Western Balkans. Despite progress in the overall management of migratory flows in Bosnia and Herzegovina (BiH), the volume of migrants and the complexity in the composition of groups and vulnerable persons within these flows remains a serious challenge in terms of timely provision of basic and protection assistance, with gaps identified in the provision of tailored protection information for vulnerable categories, notably persons with disabilities or with impaired vision, and other groups with specific needs. As the lead agency for the Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) sector and co-lead of the Protection cluster and Protection Sector Working Group, IOM has a key role to play in streamlining protection services and improving the quality and coordination of the protection assistance provided to migrants and asylum seekers in Temporary Reception Centres (TRCs) in BiH. This intervention seeks to increase access to protection services and mental health and psychosocial assistance, as well as direct assistance to persons with protection risks and needs, such as those with disabilities or serious medical conditions, potential victims of trafficking, victims and survivors of Gender-Based Violence, and unaccompanied children.</narrative>
  </description>
